# sbx TLS-intercepting proxy CA — placeholder certificate.
#
# This file is installed into the browser container's OS trust store at build
# time (update-ca-certificates). Replace this with your real sbx proxy CA
# certificate before building the production image.
#
# To extract the CA from a running mitmproxy or similar proxy:
#   mitmdump --showversion   # or check your proxy's docs
#   # export cert from http://mitm.it when a browser is proxied through it
#
# To generate a fresh self-signed CA for local dev:
#   ./sbx-kit/gen-proxy-ca.sh
#   # Keep sbx-ca.key secret — do NOT commit it.
#
